{"timestamp":"2026-03-28T04:08:07.446Z","command":"gh issue create --repo systeminit/swamp-club --title \"Add createdAfter/updatedAfter date filters to extension search API\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n\nThe `GET /api/v1/extensions/search` endpoint supports text, namespace, platform, label, and contentType filters — but no date range filtering. Querying \"what's new in the last 24 hours\" currently requires either direct MongoDB access or paginating through `sort=new` results and filtering client-side.\n\n## Proposal\n\nAdd optional `createdAfter`, `createdBefore`, `updatedAfter`, and `updatedBefore` query parameters (ISO 8601 timestamps) to the search endpoint.\n\n**Example:**\n```\nGET /api/v1/extensions/search?sort=new&createdAfter=2026-03-26T00:00:00Z&perPage=100\n```\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Parse date params in `routes/api/v1/extensions/search.ts` (~5 lines)\n- Add date conditions in `buildFacetFilter()` in `mongo-extension-repository.ts` (~10 lines):\n  ```ts\n  if (createdAfter) conditions.push({ createdAt: { $gte: new Date(createdAfter) } });\n  if (createdBefore) conditions.push({ createdAt: { $lte: new Date(createdBefore) } });\n  ```\n- Existing `createdAt` and `updatedAt` indexes already cover the query\n\n## Use cases\n\n- Summary bots (daily/weekly \"what's new\" digests)\n- RSS-like integrations\n- Dashboards and analytics\n- Slack/Discord notification pipelines — without requiring raw DB credentials\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1","cwd":"/home/keeb/git/discord-project-summarizer","sessionId":"437331eb-fd31-496e-84e0-b10e746fb760"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-28T04:08:12.792Z","command":"gh issue create --repo systeminit/swamp-club --title \"Add /api/v1/extensions/recent convenience endpoint\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n\nA purpose-built endpoint for querying recently published extensions, optimized for summary bots, \"What's New\" widgets, and notification pipelines.\n\n## Proposal\n\n```\nGET /api/v1/extensions/recent?hours=24\n```\n\n**Response shape:**\n```json\n{\n  \"extensions\": [...],\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"total\": 203,\n    \"byContentType\": {\n      \"models\": 145,\n      \"workflows\": 32,\n      \"vaults\": 8,\n      \"datastores\": 5,\n      \"drivers\": 7,\n      \"reports\": 6\n    },\n    \"byNamespace\": {\n      \"@keeb\": 3,\n      \"@collective/aws\": 5\n    }\n  },\n  \"since\": \"2026-03-26T21:00:00Z\"\n}\n```\n\n## Why a separate endpoint\n\nThe general search endpoint (even with date filters from #?) works, but consumers building daily digests all need the same aggregation: group by content type, group by namespace, count totals. Doing this server-side once is better than every client re-implementing it.\n\nThis also makes a natural fit for a \"What's New\" section on the swamp.club homepage or extension browser.\n\n## Parameters\n\n| Param | Default | Description |\n|-------|---------|-------------|\n| `hours` | `24` | Lookback window |\n| `perPage` | `50` | Max extensions in the list (still paginated) |\n| `page` | `1` | Pagination |\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1","cwd":"/home/keeb/git/discord-project-summarizer","sessionId":"437331eb-fd31-496e-84e0-b10e746fb760"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-28T04:08:22.927Z","command":"gh issue create --repo systeminit/swamp-club --title \"Include author/namespace info in extension search API response\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n\nThe current `ExtensionView` returned by the search API doesn't include who published the extension. The `createdByUserId` field exists internally but never surfaces in API responses. The namespace is derivable from the extension name, but explicit author metadata would make consumer integrations much richer.\n\n## Proposal\n\nAdd `namespace` and `author` fields to the `ExtensionView` response:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"...\",\n  \"name\": \"@keeb/mongodb\",\n  \"namespace\": \"@keeb\",\n  \"author\": {\n    \"username\": \"keeb\",\n    \"displayName\": \"Keeb\"\n  },\n  \"description\": \"...\",\n  ...\n}\n```\n\n## Implementation\n\n- `namespace` can be derived from the extension name (everything before the last `/` segment) — zero-cost\n- `author` requires a join or denormalization from the user who created the extension (`createdByUserId`). Options:\n  1. **Denormalize** `authorUsername` onto the extension document at publish time (cheap, consistent with how `extension_pulls` already stores `authorUsername`)\n  2. **Join** at query time via `$lookup` (flexible but heavier)\n\nOption 1 matches the existing pattern in `extension_pulls` and keeps reads fast.\n\n## Use cases\n\n- Summary bots can report \"**@keeb** published 3 new extensions\" instead of just listing names\n- Leaderboard-style digests (\"most active publishers this week\")\n- Better attribution in notification messages (Discord, Slack, email digests)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1","cwd":"/home/keeb/git/discord-project-summarizer","sessionId":"437331eb-fd31-496e-84e0-b10e746fb760"}
